<slidia>
  <!--
    Community firmware catalogue read by Updater CE and innioasis.app.
    One <package/> entry per model. Use the generator at
    https://innioasis.app/developers.html to build entries.

    Attributes: name, brand, repo, device, devices, url, type="img",
    handler="Custom Firmware", package_name, package_name_<model>,
    package_name_<model>_type_<a|b>, package_name_<brand>_<model>,
    package_name_<brand>_<model>_type_<a|b>, asset_pattern, type_a_asset,
    type_b_asset, icon, icon_dark, image, image_dark, post_install,
    post_install2, portable_zips, derivative, info_repo, apk_repo,
    min_version, do_not_keep_data, slug, description.

    Models: device="Y2" names one model and is unchanged. devices="Y1,Y2,G5"
    names several models for one repository, so a project that ships one
    release for five players needs one line, not five. An entry may carry its
    brand as "Timmkoo/Q3" or "Timmkoo:Q3", which keeps two brands that share a
    model number apart. Any model added to this file later is read from these
    attributes; no code change is needed.

    Package names: package_name defaults to rom.zip on Y1 and rom_MODEL.zip on
    other models. A row that serves several models can name each model's ROM,
    and its Type B build, without repeating the repository:

      package_name_y1="rom.zip"          package_name_y1_type_b="rom_type_b.zip"
      package_name_y2="rom_y2.zip"       package_name_a5="rom_a5.zip"
      package_name_g5="rom_g5.zip"       package_name_timmkoo_q3="rom_q3.zip"

    The most specific declaration wins: brand + model + type, model + type,
    brand + model, model, then package_name. Attribute names are matched
    without case, so package_name_A5 works as well as package_name_a5.
    do_not_keep_data accepts true, 1 or yes. Legacy aliases still read:
    model, package, portable_zip, post_install_2, min_app_version, image_dark.
  -->

